# Git and terminal confirmation

## Commit and push

**Never** commit or push unless the user explicitly asks in that message.

- Do not commit “because the fix is done”
- Do not push after a commit unless they also asked to push
- If unsure, ask first

## Terminal

Before running **any** Shell / terminal command, **ask the user and wait for confirmation**.

- Include a short list of the command(s) you want to run and why
- Only proceed after they clearly approve
- Applies to git, installs, builds, tests, scripts, and one-off checks
